==German==

===Phrase===
'''[[Sitz]] [[im]] [[Leben]]'''

# {{idiomatic|lang=de}} ("sit in life") sociological setting

===Usage notes===
Though sometimes rendered by phrases like "life setting", "situation in life" etc. the German term ''Sitz im Leben'' is better translated by "sociological setting" or left untranslated.  As a technical term, it refers to the social setting of a text, particularly in the bible. Invented by one Hermann Gunkel, it is rarely used today even in academic context.